<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav November crude oil imports up vs October.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav November crude oil imports up vs October.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yugoslav crude oil imports in November rose to 294,892 tonnes from 189,829 tonnes in October, the Federal Statistics Office said in its latest report.</p>
<p>Crude oil imports were worth $56 million against $35 million the previous month.</p>
<p>Imports of refined oil products dropped to 34,310 tonnes from 47,258 in October and were worth $10 million against the previous month's $12 million.</p>
<p>Cummulative January-November crude imports stood at 1,098,321 tonnes and were worth $190 million.</p>
<p>In the same period, oil products imports totalled 1,056,658 tonnes worth $234 million.</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 2224305</p>
